https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hurwitz_zeta_function

Circle Packing using the Hurwitz zeta function to select subsequent circle areas (thus radii), 
with carefully selected parameters to get reasonably fast convergance. The hue starts random and 
shifts on a power scale, so the more circles generated the less it shifts.  This lets the colours kinda
match the sizes.

